IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hrq-dates`
IMPORT `hrq-core`
IMPORT `hrq-seat`

-- Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) -- worked cases for the individual's questions (hrq-seat.l4), the rules
-- (hrq-core.l4) and the dates (hrq-dates.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was
-- copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.
-- The facts are illustrative: a remand prisoner in a privately run prison, a person held in a watch-house, a child in
-- State care, a patient refused treatment at a public hospital, a tenant of a funded housing provider.
--
-- Dates worked by hand (1 January 2026 is a Thursday, so 2 March 2026 is a Monday, 7 April a Tuesday, 1 May a Friday,
-- 9 June a Tuesday):
-- * 45 business days after Monday 2 March 2026, no public holidays: Tue 3 - Fri 6 March is 4, eight full weeks to Friday
--   1 May make 44, Monday 4 May is the 45th; the earliest day is Tuesday 5 May 2026.
-- * The same, taking 3 April, 6 April and 4 May 2026 as the public holidays supplied: 42 by Friday 1 May, Monday 4 May
--   not counted, Tue 5 (43), Wed 6 (44), Thu 7 (45); the earliest day is Friday 8 May 2026.
-- * 45 business days after Tuesday 7 April 2026: Wed 8 - Fri 10 April is 3, eight full weeks to Friday 5 June make 43,
--   Mon 8 (44), Tue 9 June (45); the earliest day is Wednesday 10 June 2026. After Wednesday 8 April: the 45th is
--   Wednesday 10 June; the earliest day is Thursday 11 June 2026.
-- * 45 business days after Friday 1 May 2026: nine full weeks, the 45th is Friday 3 July; the earliest day is Saturday
--   4 July 2026.
-- * 1 year after 10 June 2025 ends on 10 June 2026; after 29 February 2024, on 28 February 2025 (fork F2).
-- * An override provision commenced 1 July 2020 is in force to the end of 1 July 2025 (fork F12); one commenced
--   29 February 2024 to the end of 28 February 2029.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`unused` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000
`no holidays` MEANS EMPTY

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 11`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Do I have human rights under the Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: an individual in Queensland has human rights (s 11(1))`
#ASSERT `Do I have human rights under the Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: only individuals have human rights; a corporation or other body has none (s 11(2))`
#ASSERT `Do I have human rights under the Act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: only individuals have human rights; a corporation or other body has none (s 11(2))`
#ASSERT `Do I have human rights under the Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not answered: s 11(1) speaks of individuals in Queensland; for an individual outside Queensland the Act does not say`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 9, 10 -- public entity`
-- ===================================================================================================================

`gov` MEANS `a government entity, such as a department or a public service office (Public Sector Act 2022, s 276)`
`employee` MEANS `a public service employee`
`police` MEANS `the Queensland Police Service, or a police officer`
`council` MEANS `a local government, a councillor or a local government employee`
`minister` MEANS `a Minister`
`statutory` MEANS `an entity established under an Act (for example a hospital and health service, a statutory authority or a public university)`
`committee` MEANS `a member of a portfolio committee of Parliament`
`staff` MEANS `a staff member or executive officer of a public entity, not otherwise covered`
`ndis` MEANS `a registered NDIS provider or registered provider of supports`
`nonstate` MEANS `a non-State police officer (for example a Commonwealth officer appointed or authorised under the Police Service Administration Act 1990)`
`assembly` MEANS `the Legislative Assembly, or a person performing functions in connection with its proceedings`
`tribunal` MEANS `a court or a tribunal`
`private` MEANS `another body or person, not set up under an Act (for example a private company running a prison, a care provider or a contractor)`

`prison` MEANS `operating a corrective services facility or another place of detention`
`health` MEANS `providing public health services`
`housing` MEANS `providing a housing service as a funded provider or the State under the Housing Act 2003`
`disability` MEANS `providing public disability services`
`other fn` MEANS `another function`

-- Arguments: kind, function, court finds public nature, for the State, administrative, works for a public entity,
-- non-State officer acting, prescribed to be, prescribed not to be, s 60 declaration.
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `gov` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a government entity (s 9(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `employee` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a public service employee (s 9(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `police` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Queensland Police Service (s 9(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `council` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a local government, a councillor or a local government employee (s 9(1)(d))`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `minister` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a Minister (s 9(1)(e))`
-- a hospital and health service providing public health services: s 10(3)(b)(ii) makes it public without a finding
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `statutory` `health` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: an entity established under an Act, performing functions of a public nature (s 9(1)(f))`
-- a statutory body doing something a court would not find public: not shown
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `statutory` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not shown: none of the kinds in s 9 fits these facts (s 9 does not close its list)`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `statutory` `other fn` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: an entity established under an Act, performing functions of a public nature (s 9(1)(f))`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `committee` `other fn` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a member of a portfolio committee, the committee acting in an administrative capacity (s 9(1)(g))`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `committee` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not shown: none of the kinds in s 9 fits these facts (s 9 does not close its list)`
-- a private company running a prison for the State: s 10(3)(a) and s 9(1)(h)
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `private` `prison` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: an entity performing functions of a public nature for the State or a public entity (s 9(1)(h))`
-- the same company not doing it for the State (the s 9(1)(h) example: a non-State school)
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `private` `prison` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not shown: none of the kinds in s 9 fits these facts (s 9 does not close its list)`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `private` `housing` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: an entity performing functions of a public nature for the State or a public entity (s 9(1)(h))`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `private` `other fn` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not shown: none of the kinds in s 9 fits these facts (s 9 does not close its list)`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `staff` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a staff member or executive officer of a public entity (s 9(1)(i))`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `staff` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not shown: none of the kinds in s 9 fits these facts (s 9 does not close its list)`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `private` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: an entity prescribed by regulation to be a public entity (s 9(1)(j))`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `ndis` `disability` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a registered provider performing functions of a public nature in the State (s 9(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `ndis` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not shown: none of the kinds in s 9 fits these facts (s 9 does not close its list)`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `nonstate` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a non-State police officer while appointed, authorised or exercising a power under State law (s 9(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `nonstate` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not shown: none of the kinds in s 9 fits these facts (s 9 does not close its list)`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `private` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: an entity that chose to be subject to the obligations, by a declaration in force under s 60 (s 9(3))`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `assembly` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the Legislative Assembly, or a person performing functions in connection with its proceedings, except when acting in an administrative capacity (s 9(4)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `tribunal` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a court or tribunal, except when acting in an administrative capacity (s 9(4)(b))`
-- a court deciding a case is excluded even though its function might be public
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `tribunal` `other fn` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a court or tribunal, except when acting in an administrative capacity (s 9(4)(b))`
-- a court acting administratively, its function of a public nature: taken under (f) (fork F5)
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `tribunal` `other fn` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: an entity established under an Act, performing functions of a public nature (s 9(1)(f))`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `tribunal` `other fn` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not shown: none of the kinds in s 9 fits these facts (s 9 does not close its list)`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `assembly` `other fn` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: an entity established under an Act, performing functions of a public nature (s 9(1)(f))`
-- an exclusion by regulation beats every head, even a department and a s 60 declaration
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `gov` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: an entity prescribed by regulation not to be a public entity (s 9(4)(c))`
#ASSERT `Is the body a public entity` `private` `prison` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: an entity prescribed by regulation not to be a public entity (s 9(4)(c))`
#ASSERT `is a public entity` (`s 9 -- public entity` `police` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a public entity` (`s 9 -- public entity` `private` `other fn` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)))
-- s 10(3) listed functions need no finding; another function takes the finding
#ASSERT `s 10 -- of a public nature` `providing emergency services` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 10 -- of a public nature` `providing public transport` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 10 -- of a public nature` `providing public education, including public tertiary or vocational education` FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 10 -- of a public nature` `other fn` FALSE))
#ASSERT `s 10 -- of a public nature` `other fn` TRUE

